1
00:00:41,750 --> 00:00:43,167
THIS DRAMA RECREATES HISTORICAL FIGURES
AND EVENTS WITH ADDED IMAGINATION

2
00:00:43,168 --> 00:00:44,668
CHILD ACTOR AND ANIMAL SCENES WERE MADE
WITH GUARDIANS' AND EXPERTS' HELP,

3
00:00:44,669 --> 00:00:45,670
AND GENERATIVE AI WAS USED IN SOME SCENES

4
00:00:49,257 --> 00:00:55,180
<i>On this land, Goguryeo, Baekje, and Silla
fought fiercely for hundreds of years.</i>

5
00:00:56,306 --> 00:00:59,308
<i>Meanwhile, even Tang,
which unified the continent,</i>

6
00:00:59,309 --> 00:01:00,727
<i>set its sights on this land.</i>

7
00:01:01,436 --> 00:01:06,357
<i>In 642, Silla was cornered
by the threats of Baekje and Goguryeo.</i>

8
00:01:07,150 --> 00:01:11,446
<i>Inside, Jingol nobles
fought over the throne.</i>

9
00:01:12,781 --> 00:01:18,244
<i>The enemy was both outside and within.</i>

10
00:01:21,790 --> 00:01:24,167
SEORABEOL, SILLA, 642

11
00:01:47,732 --> 00:01:49,025
Blaming the wind?

12
00:01:49,859 --> 00:01:52,111
- I'm reading the wind, brother.
- What?

13
00:01:52,112 --> 00:01:53,112
KIM BEOP-MIN

14
00:01:53,113 --> 00:01:55,281
- You're reading the wind?
- Brother.

15
00:01:55,990 --> 00:01:57,366
KIM IN-MUN

16
00:01:57,367 --> 00:01:59,160
They say

17
00:01:59,994 --> 00:02:02,664
an arrow flies true
when shot to save, not to kill.

18
00:02:07,418 --> 00:02:08,253
Save what?

19
00:02:14,801 --> 00:02:15,635
The country.

20
00:02:19,347 --> 00:02:21,182
Hit!

21
00:02:22,100 --> 00:02:24,060
Hit!

22
00:02:57,719 --> 00:02:59,637
Miss!

23
00:03:00,555 --> 00:03:02,140
Miss!

24
00:03:03,850 --> 00:03:06,644
Why shoot an arrow to save a dead country?

25
00:03:07,812 --> 00:03:09,314
Going on about the country again?

26
00:03:10,440 --> 00:03:12,524
If you're not confident, just say so.

27
00:03:12,525 --> 00:03:14,067
Anyway, a promise is a promise.

28
00:03:14,068 --> 00:03:15,320
That bow is mine now.

29
00:03:16,821 --> 00:03:20,033
How can I defeat you
when you read the wind? Huh?

30
00:03:20,742 --> 00:03:22,493
The bow of the wind's divine archer.

31
00:03:23,578 --> 00:03:24,746
Let me try it too!

32
00:03:25,830 --> 00:03:27,581
Here we go again.

33
00:03:27,582 --> 00:03:28,666
Brother!

34
00:03:40,553 --> 00:03:42,805
KIM CHUN-CHU (SILLA MINISTER OF DEFENSE)

35
00:04:08,623 --> 00:04:10,541
Brother! Just how far are you going?

36
00:05:32,749 --> 00:05:33,833
Baek-ryong!

37
00:05:35,585 --> 00:05:36,836
Chun-chu.

38
00:05:38,046 --> 00:05:39,004
What are you doing?

39
00:05:39,005 --> 00:05:40,172
Get a physician!

40
00:05:40,173 --> 00:05:42,967
- We must save the general. Now!
- Yes!

41
00:05:57,565 --> 00:06:01,277
We must stop the plague!
Burn all the bodies! That's an order!

42
00:06:10,953 --> 00:06:12,830
Did we lose to Baekje again?

43
00:06:35,436 --> 00:06:39,107
Those Baekje scum took our fortress
and killed them all.

44
00:06:40,983 --> 00:06:42,735
How could all those fortresses...

45
00:06:44,237 --> 00:06:45,488
Daeya Fortress?

46
00:06:47,782 --> 00:06:49,158
Now only Daeya Fortress remains.

47
00:06:51,702 --> 00:06:53,121
That scoundrel Kim Pum-seok...

48
00:07:06,092 --> 00:07:08,260
You abandoned the country and ran?

49
00:07:08,261 --> 00:07:10,011
You cowards!

50
00:07:10,012 --> 00:07:12,472
- Drop dead!
- Kill them!

51
00:07:12,473 --> 00:07:14,307
Drop dead!

52
00:07:14,308 --> 00:07:15,726
Kill them right now!

53
00:07:18,855 --> 00:07:20,440
We...!

54
00:07:21,149 --> 00:07:23,776
We've fought as much as we could!

55
00:07:24,610 --> 00:07:27,738
The generals only send us to our deaths.

56
00:07:28,781 --> 00:07:32,200
Could you endure that?

57
00:07:32,201 --> 00:07:35,078
I've been wronged!

58
00:07:35,079 --> 00:07:39,125
Silla does not forgive
those who retreat from the battlefield.

59
00:07:39,709 --> 00:07:41,377
- Behead them!
- Yes!

60
00:07:58,644 --> 00:08:00,938
If we step back, we're all going to die.

61
00:08:02,023 --> 00:08:04,066
Goguryeo, Baekje, even the Wae...

62
00:08:05,526 --> 00:08:07,403
We're the ones with nowhere to run.

63
00:08:11,282 --> 00:08:12,116
Hell.

64
00:08:16,537 --> 00:08:18,955
No...

65
00:08:18,956 --> 00:08:19,998
Honey!

66
00:08:19,999 --> 00:08:22,919
Honey...

67
00:08:23,753 --> 00:08:25,837
Please spare him this once.

68
00:08:25,838 --> 00:08:28,173
Please spare him this once!

69
00:08:28,174 --> 00:08:31,093
Please spare him...

70
00:08:59,872 --> 00:09:01,874
Why didn't you light the beacon?!

71
00:09:02,375 --> 00:09:03,334
Why did Kim Pum-seok...

72
00:09:03,918 --> 00:09:05,920
We were ambushed
before we could light the beacon.

73
00:09:06,504 --> 00:09:09,382
There must be people in the fortress
who colluded with Baekje.

74
00:09:10,132 --> 00:09:10,967
Those Gaya scum...

75
00:09:12,426 --> 00:09:14,095
They must be behind it.

76
00:09:15,846 --> 00:09:17,597
That's a dangerous thing to say.

77
00:09:17,598 --> 00:09:19,016
Don't jump to conclusions.

78
00:09:19,976 --> 00:09:21,184
Isn't it obvious?

79
00:09:21,185 --> 00:09:22,811
Where is Sokham Fortress?

80
00:09:22,812 --> 00:09:24,438
Wasn't it their land to begin with?

81
00:09:24,939 --> 00:09:28,192
Even the soldiers guarding the gate
were all from Gaya.

82
00:09:29,318 --> 00:09:32,363
The beacon never going up,
the gates being opened,

83
00:09:33,114 --> 00:09:34,699
not sending reinforcements...

84
00:09:35,283 --> 00:09:37,159
it was all the work of those Gaya scum!

85
00:09:42,790 --> 00:09:44,624
Did you see the Gaya colluding with them?

86
00:09:44,625 --> 00:09:45,918
Must I see it to know?!

87
00:09:46,586 --> 00:09:48,379
They will betray us at any moment!

88
00:09:50,464 --> 00:09:52,300
We must report this
to Her Majesty at once.

89
00:09:54,719 --> 00:09:55,886
Baek-ryong.

90
00:09:57,513 --> 00:09:59,432
Why did you come to me?

91
00:10:01,726 --> 00:10:02,685
Who cares for Silla

92
00:10:04,103 --> 00:10:05,771
like Kim Chun-chu?

93
00:10:07,481 --> 00:10:08,482
If anyone, it's you...

94
00:10:32,632 --> 00:10:33,466
You...

95
00:10:35,176 --> 00:10:36,344
Don't tell me!

96
00:11:07,041 --> 00:11:08,834
WOLSEONG (ROYAL PALACE), SEORABEOL, SILLA

97
00:11:19,136 --> 00:11:21,180
Her Majesty is arriving!

98
00:11:33,150 --> 00:11:35,443
KIM JIN-JU (SILLA MINISTER, JINGOL)

99
00:11:35,444 --> 00:11:37,779
YEOMJONG (SILLA MINISTER, JINGOL)

100
00:11:37,780 --> 00:11:40,157
BIDAM (SILLA MINISTER, JINGOL)

101
00:12:00,928 --> 00:12:03,139
QUEEN SEONDEOK (27TH MONARCH OF SILLA)

102
00:12:03,889 --> 00:12:06,015
Where is the Minister of Defense?

103
00:12:06,016 --> 00:12:07,643
He is bedridden, Your Majesty.

104
00:12:15,943 --> 00:12:19,155
I'm told the Minister of Defense is ill.

105
00:12:19,822 --> 00:12:23,284
The Minister must find his strength
at a time like this.

106
00:12:24,201 --> 00:12:28,371
We've lost 40 fortresses to Baekje
and the country is on the verge of ruin,

107
00:12:28,372 --> 00:12:31,667
and the Minister is using illness
as an excuse?

108
00:12:34,044 --> 00:12:37,631
He's only human. He can fall ill.
Would the Minister be different?

109
00:12:38,424 --> 00:12:41,134
Is he truly ill,

110
00:12:41,135 --> 00:12:44,805
or is he up to some scheme again...

111
00:12:46,724 --> 00:12:48,100
Countless people

112
00:12:49,018 --> 00:12:52,437
have lost their families
and are suffering even more.

113
00:12:52,438 --> 00:12:53,981
Stop it.

114
00:12:55,900 --> 00:12:58,903
If only General Kim Yu-sin
were in Seorabeol,

115
00:12:59,945 --> 00:13:02,072
I wouldn't feel so anxious.

116
00:13:05,242 --> 00:13:06,702
General Kim Yu-sin

117
00:13:07,536 --> 00:13:10,705
has been at the border for three years
without rotation.

118
00:13:10,706 --> 00:13:13,583
Why not summon him this time?

119
00:13:13,584 --> 00:13:15,753
How can we leave
the Goguryeo border unguarded?

120
00:13:16,337 --> 00:13:18,546
I hear Go Geon-mu, King of Goguryeo,

121
00:13:18,547 --> 00:13:21,050
has focused on domestic affairs,

122
00:13:21,759 --> 00:13:23,802
and he's avoiding war.

123
00:13:25,346 --> 00:13:26,847
It's just a rumor, Your Majesty.

124
00:13:27,598 --> 00:13:30,434
Unless we're allied with Goguryeo,
we mustn't judge so easily.

125
00:13:31,519 --> 00:13:34,897
If Goguryeo comes down from the north,
that will truly be the end.

126
00:13:48,661 --> 00:13:51,413
For the sake of Silla,

127
00:13:52,456 --> 00:13:54,375
I intend to hold a Buddhist rite.

128
00:13:56,335 --> 00:13:59,296
Please look after your health,
Your Majesty.

129
00:14:10,766 --> 00:14:13,519
Harping on about Buddha again...

130
00:14:23,946 --> 00:14:25,072
Lord Bidam.

131
00:14:26,699 --> 00:14:29,702
It seems things have happened
just as you said.

132
00:14:30,202 --> 00:14:31,035
What's going on?

133
00:14:31,036 --> 00:14:35,540
There are rumors that Baek-ryong
went to Kim Chun-chu's house.

134
00:14:35,541 --> 00:14:38,334
General Baek-ryong of Sokham Fortress?
And?

135
00:14:38,335 --> 00:14:41,297
No one has seen Baek-ryong since.

136
00:14:41,839 --> 00:14:44,465
He went in, but couldn't get out.

137
00:14:44,466 --> 00:14:46,218
Doesn't that mean he's dead?

138
00:14:47,678 --> 00:14:50,681
If Baek-ryong were dead,
Chun-chu would have raised a ruckus, man!

139
00:14:51,181 --> 00:14:55,602
Chun-chu and Baek-ryong were the closest
of the three of us. Childhood friends.

140
00:14:55,603 --> 00:14:58,898
And he's hiding that fact?

141
00:14:59,815 --> 00:15:00,649
Why?

142
00:15:01,317 --> 00:15:04,611
Baek-ryong would never leave his fortress,

143
00:15:04,612 --> 00:15:07,865
yet he abandoned the fortress
and came to Chun-chu.

144
00:15:09,617 --> 00:15:11,951
Doesn't that mean he found something huge?

145
00:15:11,952 --> 00:15:16,373
Didn't General Baek-ryong
despise people of Gaya descent terribly?

146
00:15:16,957 --> 00:15:20,543
If Baek-ryong risked retreating
to come here,

147
00:15:20,544 --> 00:15:24,172
he must have found something fatal
to those of Gaya descent, right?

148
00:15:24,173 --> 00:15:26,382
There's already a lot of talk in Seorabeol

149
00:15:26,383 --> 00:15:29,427
that people of Gaya descent
are colluding with Baekje,

150
00:15:29,428 --> 00:15:31,221
and that Baek-ryong tried to report it.

151
00:15:39,063 --> 00:15:44,068
So Baek-ryong came to tell him,
only to be killed by Chun-chu himself?

152
00:15:47,863 --> 00:15:49,113
Why?

153
00:15:49,114 --> 00:15:51,824
Chun-chu's wife is the sister
of General Kim Yu-sin,

154
00:15:51,825 --> 00:15:53,618
who is of Gaya descent,

155
00:15:53,619 --> 00:15:57,331
and their children also have Gaya blood,

156
00:15:57,831 --> 00:16:01,000
so did Chun-chu, to protect
his Gaya-descended family,

157
00:16:01,001 --> 00:16:03,086
kill Baek-ryong?

158
00:16:03,087 --> 00:16:04,588
The mighty Kim Chun-chu?

159
00:16:08,717 --> 00:16:11,135
Take off your robes and go write plays.

160
00:16:11,136 --> 00:16:13,430
Oh, you fools.

161
00:16:14,807 --> 00:16:15,641
Jin-ju.

162
00:16:17,434 --> 00:16:19,352
You know, you're a genius.

163
00:16:19,353 --> 00:16:20,688
You just realized that?

164
00:16:22,439 --> 00:16:25,650
Then shouldn't we quickly seize
Kim Chun-chu and interrogate him?

165
00:16:25,651 --> 00:16:28,529
This is a perfect opportunity
to shake Chun-chu and the Queen!

166
00:16:29,989 --> 00:16:32,116
The truth doesn't matter.

167
00:16:32,700 --> 00:16:35,536
What matters is what people believe.

168
00:16:37,162 --> 00:16:40,624
Just gather plenty of ministers
to fan this spark.

169
00:16:42,042 --> 00:16:43,335
Then the fire

170
00:16:44,378 --> 00:16:46,964
will swallow Kim Chun-chu on its own.

171
00:16:51,802 --> 00:16:53,219
Not Chun-chu, though.

172
00:16:53,220 --> 00:16:56,348
Would you go after a man over a joke, huh?

173
00:16:57,641 --> 00:16:58,976
Which side are you on?

174
00:17:05,566 --> 00:17:08,360
Lord Chun-chu has sent word
to you, my lord.

175
00:17:17,911 --> 00:17:20,497
He wants us to watch a play together?

176
00:17:24,376 --> 00:17:26,003
Kim Chun-chu.

177
00:17:37,973 --> 00:17:39,475
NATIONAL ACADEMY RECRUITMENT NOTICE

178
00:17:42,269 --> 00:17:44,938
I hear Tang's Emperor Li Shimin
opened a national academy.

179
00:17:46,398 --> 00:17:48,567
Talent from everywhere
is gathering in Tang now.

180
00:17:50,360 --> 00:17:52,154
Learning and interacting there

181
00:17:52,738 --> 00:17:54,572
will be an irreplaceable opportunity.

182
00:17:54,573 --> 00:17:58,243
Just for a little more land,
meaningless corpses are burning.

183
00:17:59,119 --> 00:17:59,953
It's as though

184
00:18:01,246 --> 00:18:03,373
they were born only to die.

185
00:18:04,416 --> 00:18:05,250
But...

186
00:18:06,794 --> 00:18:08,336
as your sons,

187
00:18:08,337 --> 00:18:10,714
are we to flee death and go to Tang?

188
00:18:11,715 --> 00:18:13,967
Not everyone needs to die
on the battlefield.

189
00:18:14,802 --> 00:18:16,386
Someone has to raise a sword.

190
00:18:17,179 --> 00:18:19,264
Someone has to go to a wider world

191
00:18:20,015 --> 00:18:22,434
and find a way to save the country.

192
00:18:28,273 --> 00:18:31,777
If you won't go to Tang,
even you must go to battle.

193
00:18:32,736 --> 00:18:35,613
But you can't even shoot a bow properly.

194
00:18:35,614 --> 00:18:37,199
You'll be a corpse in no time.

195
00:18:38,325 --> 00:18:41,495
It would waste the soldiers' effort
to clear away your body.

196
00:18:42,287 --> 00:18:44,665
Who removed General Baek-ryong's body?

197
00:18:45,999 --> 00:18:48,627
Was that also for the sake of the country?

198
00:18:56,510 --> 00:18:57,886
The decision has been made.

199
00:18:59,888 --> 00:19:02,098
I'm going nowhere.

200
00:19:02,099 --> 00:19:03,433
Be it war or Tang,

201
00:19:04,017 --> 00:19:06,477
the greedy would only use and discard me.

202
00:19:06,478 --> 00:19:07,980
I won't do that!

203
00:19:08,897 --> 00:19:09,731
Brother.

204
00:19:10,357 --> 00:19:13,067
Baekje kills Silla,
and Silla kills Baekje.

205
00:19:13,068 --> 00:19:15,154
Haven't we fought this war for 200 years?

206
00:19:35,382 --> 00:19:36,216
Listen to me.

207
00:19:39,052 --> 00:19:43,307
Whether you go to Tang, serve in battle,
or refuse it all...

208
00:19:45,601 --> 00:19:47,019
you are my son.

209
00:19:48,270 --> 00:19:50,189
That will never change.

210
00:19:56,528 --> 00:19:58,572
Your thoughts and mine
are not so different.

211
00:19:59,698 --> 00:20:02,743
Ending this cruel karma
of killing one another

212
00:20:04,411 --> 00:20:05,704
is our destiny.

213
00:20:16,256 --> 00:20:19,551
Beop-min, you will go to Tang,
and In-mun will go with me to Daeya.

214
00:20:20,260 --> 00:20:21,094
Yes.

215
00:20:31,063 --> 00:20:31,897
Brother!

216
00:20:53,794 --> 00:20:56,462
I lost my husband
before our wedding night,

217
00:20:56,463 --> 00:20:58,674
What joy is left in life for me?

218
00:21:00,050 --> 00:21:03,262
Pleasures of the flesh can be found again.

219
00:21:03,887 --> 00:21:08,058
If your husband is dead,
you can bring in another husband.

220
00:21:09,351 --> 00:21:12,186
The high and mighty are divided,
squabbling,

221
00:21:12,187 --> 00:21:15,856
while commoners die on the battlefield
and only women are left.

222
00:21:15,857 --> 00:21:17,067
Where from?

223
00:21:18,068 --> 00:21:18,902
Your Majesty.

224
00:21:19,987 --> 00:21:23,990
The country has run out of men.

225
00:21:23,991 --> 00:21:27,828
How can we stop our enemies now?

226
00:21:30,372 --> 00:21:31,206
Then I'll

227
00:21:32,082 --> 00:21:34,543
make you all bear sons, won't I?

228
00:21:38,297 --> 00:21:39,797
You too!

229
00:21:39,798 --> 00:21:42,091
No matter how many die,

230
00:21:42,092 --> 00:21:46,972
I'll keep making you bear sons!

231
00:21:47,806 --> 00:21:49,224
Isn't this fun to watch?

232
00:21:52,811 --> 00:21:55,147
Funnier still, you invited me
to this play.

233
00:21:56,106 --> 00:21:59,359
Isn't this play mocking your grandfather,
King Jinji?

234
00:22:01,111 --> 00:22:02,987
Why did you invite me here?

235
00:22:02,988 --> 00:22:06,198
I'm going to catch them all
and make sure they never play again.

236
00:22:06,199 --> 00:22:08,952
You lunatics! You rascals!

237
00:22:10,537 --> 00:22:11,872
It's fine.

238
00:22:12,998 --> 00:22:16,209
Even the heavyhearted
need to vent their grief.

239
00:22:16,793 --> 00:22:19,796
Are you proud of an ancestor
who was deposed?

240
00:22:20,547 --> 00:22:21,381
Of course not.

241
00:22:23,633 --> 00:22:27,304
But seeing that made me think a lot.

242
00:22:28,555 --> 00:22:31,767
The people on the frontier
are beheaded by the enemy.

243
00:22:32,392 --> 00:22:36,271
The people in the capital
are starving to death right now.

244
00:22:37,272 --> 00:22:40,358
We must unite as one and save the country.

245
00:22:42,778 --> 00:22:44,654
Otherwise, only destruction awaits...

246
00:22:46,823 --> 00:22:49,242
Are you saying we're causing division?

247
00:22:50,535 --> 00:22:51,787
It is division.

248
00:22:53,121 --> 00:22:56,666
Have you ever reached a unanimous decision
in the Hwabaek Council?

249
00:22:57,584 --> 00:22:59,211
By unanimous vote,

250
00:23:01,088 --> 00:23:03,422
wasn't King Jinji deposed?

251
00:23:03,423 --> 00:23:05,299
Not about deposing him.

252
00:23:05,300 --> 00:23:07,260
I mean uniting for the country.

253
00:23:07,844 --> 00:23:11,556
Of all people,
Kim Chun-chu talking about harmony?

254
00:23:12,599 --> 00:23:14,726
Even a passing dog would laugh.

255
00:23:15,936 --> 00:23:18,104
You were blinded by your lust for victory.

256
00:23:18,105 --> 00:23:20,565
You saw me surrounded by Baekje troops,

257
00:23:21,399 --> 00:23:24,653
yet cared only about opening the gates!

258
00:23:36,331 --> 00:23:37,541
Chun-chu!

259
00:23:38,333 --> 00:23:39,209
Help me!

260
00:24:12,826 --> 00:24:13,702
That's why...

261
00:24:16,079 --> 00:24:17,414
to this day,

262
00:24:18,832 --> 00:24:22,544
I can't get rid of this cane!

263
00:24:29,676 --> 00:24:30,594
Bidam.

264
00:24:31,678 --> 00:24:34,556
Back then, Chun-chu had no choice
if he wanted to survive.

265
00:24:46,443 --> 00:24:49,029
Only you would remember

266
00:24:50,155 --> 00:24:52,490
what the truth really was.

267
00:25:12,719 --> 00:25:15,263
The fear you felt then,

268
00:25:16,848 --> 00:25:17,933
the confusion.

269
00:25:19,726 --> 00:25:20,602
I know it well.

270
00:25:22,103 --> 00:25:22,938
That's a lie!

271
00:25:23,939 --> 00:25:26,358
Chun-chu, you're a man without fear.

272
00:25:27,317 --> 00:25:31,820
You were thinking about your next move
even as your comrades were beheaded.

273
00:25:31,821 --> 00:25:32,739
No, I wasn't.

274
00:25:33,615 --> 00:25:34,574
You're wrong.

275
00:25:35,784 --> 00:25:39,871
I'm afraid of people dying,
and I fear losing my country.

276
00:25:41,498 --> 00:25:43,500
And for your pain, my former comrade,

277
00:25:44,626 --> 00:25:46,211
I truly feel sorry.

278
00:25:47,379 --> 00:25:48,505
What?

279
00:25:50,382 --> 00:25:52,549
If we can't protect Daeya Fortress now,

280
00:25:52,550 --> 00:25:55,428
Baekje's blade will cut deep
into Seorabeol.

281
00:25:56,930 --> 00:25:58,765
I will go to Daeya Fortress,

282
00:25:59,557 --> 00:26:02,435
and if Kim Pum-seok is guilty,

283
00:26:03,144 --> 00:26:04,479
I'll die there with my son.

284
00:26:13,405 --> 00:26:15,532
They say the real motive comes last.

285
00:26:17,200 --> 00:26:20,412
In the end, you want more troops
for Daeya Fortress, don't you?

286
00:26:26,584 --> 00:26:28,794
Your 500 household troops, Bidam,

287
00:26:28,795 --> 00:26:30,629
and Lord Jin-ju's 300 household troops.

288
00:26:30,630 --> 00:26:31,923
We desperately need them.

289
00:26:32,966 --> 00:26:33,800
Please

290
00:26:34,926 --> 00:26:36,469
join forces with me.

291
00:26:37,345 --> 00:26:41,891
With Goguryeo threatening us,
you'd pull Seorabeol's troops at will...

292
00:26:42,809 --> 00:26:43,768
You're insane.

293
00:26:46,021 --> 00:26:49,190
Your heart may be with Daeya Fortress,
where your daughter is,

294
00:26:49,774 --> 00:26:50,984
but mine is with Seorabeol.

295
00:26:52,152 --> 00:26:53,862
Isn't it the royal capital?

296
00:26:54,821 --> 00:26:58,325
I'm sure the Queen, who dotes on you,
feels the same.

297
00:27:05,749 --> 00:27:07,667
If you want it that badly,

298
00:27:08,835 --> 00:27:10,170
try getting on your knees.

299
00:27:12,964 --> 00:27:14,841
I need to see for myself

300
00:27:15,759 --> 00:27:17,594
how desperate you truly are!

301
00:27:46,456 --> 00:27:48,208
Chun-chu, my dear man.

302
00:27:58,676 --> 00:28:00,178
You're good at acting!

303
00:28:02,222 --> 00:28:05,058
You're the one putting on the real show!

304
00:28:31,960 --> 00:28:35,672
Your face looks sadder
than your father on his knees.

305
00:28:37,048 --> 00:28:40,969
You've still got a long way to go
to be like your father, boy.

306
00:29:13,376 --> 00:29:16,004
Tell me this instant
where the body was buried!

307
00:29:17,589 --> 00:29:19,507
That's...

308
00:29:20,759 --> 00:29:24,971
Lord Chun-chu took
only the servants he could trust.

309
00:29:30,185 --> 00:29:32,937
LIAODONG, GOGURYEO, 642

310
00:29:42,280 --> 00:29:43,572
Did you hear that?

311
00:29:43,573 --> 00:29:45,824
The Gyeonggwan built after defeating Sui

312
00:29:45,825 --> 00:29:46,742
will be torn down.

313
00:29:46,743 --> 00:29:47,743
LORD OF ANSI FORTRESS

314
00:29:47,744 --> 00:29:49,536
He wants to avoid a war with Tang.

315
00:29:49,537 --> 00:29:52,080
Shouldn't we go stop His Majesty
right now?

316
00:29:52,081 --> 00:29:54,000
You must not leave your fortress.

317
00:29:55,168 --> 00:29:57,503
Our job is to guard Liaodong.

318
00:29:57,504 --> 00:29:58,421
Brother!

319
00:29:59,422 --> 00:30:00,381
I'll see you later.

320
00:30:14,103 --> 00:30:17,815
They say the Gyeonggwan and shrines
have all been torn down,

321
00:30:17,816 --> 00:30:20,360
and Chen Dade of Tang has arrived.

322
00:30:53,268 --> 00:30:55,395
GO GEON-MU (27TH KING OF GOGURYEO)

323
00:31:10,702 --> 00:31:12,662
You totally destroyed it.

324
00:31:13,705 --> 00:31:15,206
Didn't you want this?

325
00:31:15,790 --> 00:31:20,794
Since you tore down the Gyeonggwan
and shrines built after defeating Sui,

326
00:31:20,795 --> 00:31:24,673
even the people of Tang
will now regard Goguryeo as a friend.

327
00:31:24,674 --> 00:31:25,758
GO YEON-MU (GENERAL)

328
00:31:26,843 --> 00:31:31,347
I can already picture
the Emperor's delight.

329
00:31:32,724 --> 00:31:35,935
You welcomed me so warmly.
I'll put in an especially good word!

330
00:31:38,813 --> 00:31:40,064
Very well.

331
00:32:10,970 --> 00:32:12,388
GO HWAN-GWON (CROWN PRINCE)

332
00:32:15,391 --> 00:32:36,245
Long live Yeon Gaesomun!

333
00:32:37,413 --> 00:32:39,624
YEON GAESOMUN (GOGURYEO EASTERN YOKSAL)

334
00:32:41,876 --> 00:32:43,835
GEOM MO-JAM (GOGURYEO GENERAL)

335
00:32:43,836 --> 00:32:44,963
MU-HYEOK (GOGURYEO ARMY)

336
00:33:08,778 --> 00:33:09,862
It's good.

337
00:33:22,208 --> 00:33:23,334
Isn't that hoofbeats?

338
00:33:24,460 --> 00:33:25,294
It can't be...

339
00:33:26,796 --> 00:33:27,630
Impossible.

340
00:33:28,214 --> 00:33:29,881
The King of Goguryeo has decreed it,

341
00:33:29,882 --> 00:33:31,217
so all will be well.

342
00:33:46,065 --> 00:33:47,358
Don't even think of fleeing!

343
00:33:47,734 --> 00:33:50,695
Who would dare make an enemy of the Tang?

344
00:34:04,917 --> 00:34:06,294
Seize them!

345
00:35:14,153 --> 00:35:18,199
We defeated Sui!

346
00:36:19,468 --> 00:36:20,969
DESTROYER OF THE GYEONGGWAN

347
00:36:20,970 --> 00:36:23,389
TANG PEOPLE, ENEMIES OF GOGURYEO

348
00:36:38,196 --> 00:36:39,029
Your Majesty.

349
00:36:39,030 --> 00:36:43,701
King Uija of Baekje has secretly
sent his envoy, Seong-chung.

350
00:36:46,454 --> 00:36:49,665
King Uija sent an envoy?

351
00:36:55,129 --> 00:36:59,716
You want us to join Baekje
in attacking Silla?

352
00:36:59,717 --> 00:37:01,218
Yes, Your Majesty.

353
00:37:01,219 --> 00:37:02,427
SEONG-CHUNG (JWAPYEONG)

354
00:37:02,428 --> 00:37:07,016
Baekje is now sweeping forward,
and has seized 40 of Silla's fortresses.

355
00:37:07,725 --> 00:37:10,394
If Your Majesty joins forces with us,

356
00:37:11,437 --> 00:37:12,771
Silla will collapse.

357
00:37:12,772 --> 00:37:17,777
Baekje has the power to take
40 Silla fortresses on its own.

358
00:37:18,319 --> 00:37:22,073
Why do you want to borrow our power?

359
00:37:23,282 --> 00:37:25,993
Silla's fall is plain to see,

360
00:37:26,744 --> 00:37:28,704
but if Goguryeo and Baekje join forces,

361
00:37:29,372 --> 00:37:33,375
they will suffer fewer casualties
and bring Silla down sooner.

362
00:37:33,376 --> 00:37:35,086
By sacrificing Goguryeo,

363
00:37:36,170 --> 00:37:39,090
you'd spare Baekje its losses?

364
00:37:47,473 --> 00:37:48,933
For a small sacrifice,

365
00:37:49,809 --> 00:37:52,227
you can gain great benefits.

366
00:37:52,228 --> 00:37:54,272
You know that, Your Majesty, don't you?

367
00:37:54,897 --> 00:37:55,898
War is...

368
00:37:58,150 --> 00:38:00,653
no small sacrifice.

369
00:38:01,821 --> 00:38:03,364
For Baekje's greed,

370
00:38:04,198 --> 00:38:06,075
I will not shed the blood

371
00:38:07,243 --> 00:38:09,202
of Goguryeo's people.

372
00:38:09,203 --> 00:38:10,830
If Your Majesty joins us,

373
00:38:11,622 --> 00:38:14,458
- it would help Goguryeo too--
- Have a safe journey back.

374
00:38:24,844 --> 00:38:27,929
A Tang man's severed head
has been hung in the marketplace.

375
00:38:27,930 --> 00:38:30,266
What? Who did that...

376
00:38:30,850 --> 00:38:32,476
Who else?

377
00:38:33,394 --> 00:38:35,812
It's only a matter of time
before the Tang court

378
00:38:35,813 --> 00:38:37,189
learns of this.

379
00:38:43,279 --> 00:38:45,239
Tell Yeon Gaesomun to come

380
00:38:46,365 --> 00:38:48,659
to Pyongyang Fortress at once.

381
00:38:49,368 --> 00:38:50,202
Yes!

382
00:38:57,752 --> 00:39:01,087
His Majesty is too lenient
with Yeon Gaesomun.

383
00:39:01,088 --> 00:39:05,300
He strides through the throne hall
as if the world were his!

384
00:39:05,301 --> 00:39:06,593
Yeon Gaesomun,

385
00:39:06,594 --> 00:39:10,056
that man will surely commit treason,
Your Highness.

386
00:39:11,682 --> 00:39:12,767
I swear

387
00:39:13,476 --> 00:39:15,353
I will behead that wretch!

388
00:40:14,912 --> 00:40:17,832
Time flies.

389
00:40:18,624 --> 00:40:22,503
It's been two years
since you became Eastern Yoksal.

390
00:40:28,217 --> 00:40:31,178
I told you it was best to disband
the old soldiers,

391
00:40:32,221 --> 00:40:33,722
but they remained...

392
00:40:35,599 --> 00:40:39,812
and they are privately comforting
the people on your behalf.

393
00:40:40,688 --> 00:40:45,860
If Your Majesty insists they be disbanded,
I will do so immediately.

394
00:40:48,320 --> 00:40:50,780
Send the old soldiers back to their homes.

395
00:40:50,781 --> 00:40:51,949
Let them rest.

396
00:40:53,784 --> 00:40:54,952
Goguryeo

397
00:40:55,953 --> 00:40:57,872
has fought for far too long.

398
00:40:58,539 --> 00:41:02,209
For those who grew old in that war,

399
00:41:03,085 --> 00:41:06,464
I want to give them the gift of rest.

400
00:41:07,173 --> 00:41:08,883
I will do as you say.

401
00:41:12,470 --> 00:41:13,971
And...

402
00:41:15,222 --> 00:41:17,057
Why does your Eastern Army

403
00:41:17,766 --> 00:41:19,560
keep growing?

404
00:41:20,853 --> 00:41:24,523
Rather than have those loyal soldiers
go to war with Tang

405
00:41:25,024 --> 00:41:26,150
and lose their lives,

406
00:41:26,859 --> 00:41:32,615
leaving widows and fatherless children
weeping tears of blood,

407
00:41:33,741 --> 00:41:37,912
wouldn't peace with Tang be better?

408
00:41:43,792 --> 00:41:45,294
What I desperately need now

409
00:41:46,420 --> 00:41:49,381
is a subject who will speak frankly.

410
00:41:56,055 --> 00:41:57,097
Your Majesty.

411
00:41:58,724 --> 00:42:01,059
You, the sovereign who crushed Sui,

412
00:42:01,060 --> 00:42:05,105
how can you bow your head so easily?

413
00:42:06,482 --> 00:42:08,107
Every ruler

414
00:42:08,108 --> 00:42:10,610
who unified the Central Plains
invaded neighboring countries.

415
00:42:10,611 --> 00:42:12,238
Surely you know that?

416
00:42:13,489 --> 00:42:18,159
The conquered are left wretched,
naked, and starving,

417
00:42:18,160 --> 00:42:22,080
while the conquerors
swagger about as heroes with their spoils.

418
00:42:22,081 --> 00:42:23,707
That is the way of this world.

419
00:42:25,125 --> 00:42:25,960
Now,

420
00:42:26,752 --> 00:42:28,879
the only thing left for that thief

421
00:42:30,339 --> 00:42:32,674
is our Goguryeo, Your Majesty.

422
00:42:32,675 --> 00:42:34,593
That's why I seek peace,

423
00:42:35,928 --> 00:42:38,180
to give them no pretext for war

424
00:42:39,014 --> 00:42:40,640
and let our worn-out people recover.

425
00:42:40,641 --> 00:42:42,059
Don't you see?

426
00:42:43,561 --> 00:42:47,523
We defeated Sui,
but what did we gain?

427
00:42:48,107 --> 00:42:52,403
Only ruined land
and starving people.

428
00:42:54,947 --> 00:42:55,781
Wait.

429
00:42:57,658 --> 00:43:00,201
Our time will come.

430
00:43:00,202 --> 00:43:05,165
Li Shimin has a massive army prepared,
eager to invade

431
00:43:06,000 --> 00:43:07,166
as soon as possible.

432
00:43:07,167 --> 00:43:08,836
Didn't I tell you

433
00:43:09,837 --> 00:43:11,796
I'm making peace to hold that army back?

434
00:43:11,797 --> 00:43:15,926
How can someone who seeks peace
destroy the Gyeonggwan

435
00:43:17,303 --> 00:43:21,307
and send spies disguised as envoys
to draw maps?

436
00:43:22,016 --> 00:43:26,312
They are deceiving you
and will surely invade.

437
00:43:27,605 --> 00:43:29,606
Peace is an illusion.

438
00:43:29,607 --> 00:43:32,693
Strike them
instead of trusting them, Your Majesty.

439
00:43:33,193 --> 00:43:37,948
The strategy you used against Sui,
you can use it again.

440
00:43:38,449 --> 00:43:40,491
First strike Yingzhou

441
00:43:40,492 --> 00:43:42,411
and provoke them, Your Majesty.

442
00:43:45,664 --> 00:43:47,750
Would he fall for the same trick?

443
00:43:49,251 --> 00:43:51,253
Do you take Li Shimin for a fool?

444
00:43:52,755 --> 00:43:56,591
Li Shimin has fought hundreds of battles
and never lost a single one.

445
00:43:56,592 --> 00:43:58,968
Don't you know he's a heavenly strategist?

446
00:43:58,969 --> 00:44:01,929
Your Majesty, too, has never suffered
a single defeat,

447
00:44:01,930 --> 00:44:05,768
and is this nation's hero.

448
00:44:25,204 --> 00:44:26,789
In a forest...

449
00:44:28,916 --> 00:44:33,462
lived a leopard who thought himself
king of the world and ruled over

450
00:44:34,296 --> 00:44:35,506
all the creatures.

451
00:44:37,800 --> 00:44:38,634
But...

452
00:44:39,968 --> 00:44:41,095
one day, you see...

453
00:44:44,181 --> 00:44:45,516
in that forest,

454
00:44:46,558 --> 00:44:48,185
he ran into a tiger

455
00:44:48,769 --> 00:44:50,687
and got the shock of his life.

456
00:44:51,397 --> 00:44:53,482
He had never dreamed

457
00:44:54,316 --> 00:44:57,860
that a creature bigger than himself
and so fearsome

458
00:44:57,861 --> 00:45:00,364
could exist in this world.

459
00:45:13,502 --> 00:45:16,422
So that leopard began to dream.

460
00:45:17,381 --> 00:45:18,841
"I am a tiger."

461
00:45:19,675 --> 00:45:22,428
"I must become a real tiger."

462
00:45:23,262 --> 00:45:24,972
Then he trained himself.

463
00:45:25,806 --> 00:45:29,309
Enduring the pain, again and again,

464
00:45:30,144 --> 00:45:32,603
he finally became a real tiger.

465
00:45:32,604 --> 00:45:36,733
No, he became so fearsome that even
a real tiger would tremble...

466
00:45:38,402 --> 00:45:43,407
He became a very brave
and mighty beast, Your Majesty.

467
00:46:04,636 --> 00:46:05,762
What?

468
00:46:06,597 --> 00:46:08,223
"He became a real tiger"?

469
00:46:16,690 --> 00:46:18,192
Just by dreaming?

470
00:46:21,695 --> 00:46:22,529
In truth,

471
00:46:23,947 --> 00:46:25,240
that leopard

472
00:46:25,908 --> 00:46:27,700
was a tiger from the start.

473
00:46:27,701 --> 00:46:29,495
He was the only one

474
00:46:30,496 --> 00:46:32,164
who didn't know.

475
00:46:39,004 --> 00:46:43,425
And that is none other than
our Goguryeo, and at its center

476
00:46:45,135 --> 00:46:46,678
stands Your Majesty.

477
00:46:58,899 --> 00:47:01,610
I had my worries,

478
00:47:03,028 --> 00:47:05,322
but seeing your sincerity today

479
00:47:06,698 --> 00:47:08,158
reassures me more than ever.

480
00:47:11,745 --> 00:47:16,333
I want you to take charge
of the vital Liaodong region.

481
00:47:18,502 --> 00:47:20,419
Go to Liaodong,

482
00:47:20,420 --> 00:47:23,173
oversee the great works
of the Cheolli Jangseong,

483
00:47:24,383 --> 00:47:28,220
and prepare to attack
Tang's Yingzhou.

484
00:47:35,978 --> 00:47:37,229
As you command!

485
00:47:39,606 --> 00:47:41,066
I shall carry it out.

486
00:47:42,776 --> 00:47:44,444
There's not a moment to lose,

487
00:47:45,153 --> 00:47:47,488
so once the farewell ceremony is done,

488
00:47:47,489 --> 00:47:49,157
go to Liaodong at once...

489
00:47:51,118 --> 00:47:52,452
and accomplish this task.

490
00:48:23,066 --> 00:48:24,568
Brother, what is it you want?

491
00:48:25,402 --> 00:48:28,196
A peaceful world? A beautiful world?

492
00:48:31,241 --> 00:48:32,075
In-mun.

493
00:48:32,868 --> 00:48:35,162
Must one live hoping for something?

494
00:48:37,205 --> 00:48:39,791
I'm asking if you ever think
of helping Father.

495
00:48:41,418 --> 00:48:44,962
Among Jingol nobles
who put themselves before the country,

496
00:48:44,963 --> 00:48:47,840
do you even try to
understand Father, who fights alone,

497
00:48:47,841 --> 00:48:49,509
even a little?

498
00:48:50,969 --> 00:48:51,969
Shouldn't we help Father

499
00:48:51,970 --> 00:48:55,265
and somehow build the strength
to get through this situation?

500
00:48:59,311 --> 00:49:00,603
Answer me.

501
00:49:00,604 --> 00:49:02,521
Everyone is fighting their own war!

502
00:49:02,522 --> 00:49:03,440
But you, brother...

503
00:49:11,323 --> 00:49:12,282
You go to Tang.

504
00:49:13,283 --> 00:49:14,201
What?

505
00:49:15,702 --> 00:49:17,162
I'm going to Daeya Fortress.

506
00:49:18,455 --> 00:49:20,624
Will you defy Father's wishes again?

507
00:49:22,250 --> 00:49:23,669
Absolutely not.

508
00:49:24,336 --> 00:49:26,129
Gotaso married for political reasons

509
00:49:26,838 --> 00:49:30,050
and faces danger each night
at Daeya Fortress.

510
00:49:31,551 --> 00:49:33,053
I must save her.

511
00:49:52,447 --> 00:49:53,490
Your Majesty.

512
00:49:54,074 --> 00:49:56,909
Why send a dangerous man
like Yeon Gaesomun

513
00:49:56,910 --> 00:49:59,955
to distant Liaodong,
where he is beyond our control?

514
00:50:00,997 --> 00:50:02,541
If you give me your order,

515
00:50:03,709 --> 00:50:06,378
I will remove him at once

516
00:50:07,713 --> 00:50:09,589
and eliminate the root of the trouble.

517
00:50:25,188 --> 00:50:26,690
Yeon Gaesomun

518
00:50:27,774 --> 00:50:30,402
will never set foot in Liaodong.

519
00:50:35,490 --> 00:50:38,827
Yeon Gaesomun's Eastern Army
will leave for Liaodong first,

520
00:50:39,411 --> 00:50:41,996
and when Yeon Gaesomun, alone,

521
00:50:41,997 --> 00:50:45,167
finishes the farewell ceremony
and leaves Pyongyang Fortress...

522
00:50:47,711 --> 00:50:49,921
I'll kill him then.

523
00:50:55,594 --> 00:51:00,015
To avoid alarming the people,
I'll do it outside Pyongyang Fortress.

524
00:51:02,768 --> 00:51:04,644
Go Jeong-ui, lying in ambush,

525
00:51:05,353 --> 00:51:07,481
will wipe out the Eastern Army's core.

526
00:51:09,399 --> 00:51:12,110
I've only just understood your will.

527
00:51:13,904 --> 00:51:15,322
I will follow you with my life!

528
00:51:19,201 --> 00:51:20,368
This sword...

529
00:51:21,077 --> 00:51:26,041
I've carried it since I led 500 soldiers
to crush Sui's army of tens of thousands.

530
00:51:27,083 --> 00:51:28,335
It's my greatsword.

531
00:51:29,419 --> 00:51:30,504
Throughout my life,

532
00:51:31,338 --> 00:51:33,632
it has protected me and Goguryeo.

533
00:51:37,219 --> 00:51:39,763
I will give you this sword of mine.

534
00:51:41,306 --> 00:51:45,101
You must protect Goguryeo.

535
00:52:12,504 --> 00:52:14,004
I swear on this sword,

536
00:52:14,005 --> 00:52:18,969
I will surely carry out your orders!

537
00:52:23,014 --> 00:52:25,642
SASU RIVER, NORTH OF PYONGYANG FORTRESS

538
00:52:27,102 --> 00:52:29,229
SONG OF THE EASTERN ARMY
"GOGURYEO BOWS TO NO ONE"

539
00:52:29,729 --> 00:52:36,695
<i>The whole river's waters have turned red</i>

540
00:52:37,529 --> 00:52:44,494
<i>Iron armor and drums face the north wind</i>

541
00:52:45,453 --> 00:52:52,419
<i>The glory our ancestors left
Is now in our hands</i>

542
00:52:53,336 --> 00:52:54,587
GO JEONG-UI (GOGURYEO YOKSAL)

543
00:52:54,588 --> 00:53:00,927
<i>Goguryeo bows to no one</i>

544
00:53:37,547 --> 00:53:39,549
GREAT GOGURYEO

545
00:53:43,303 --> 00:53:44,387
What should I do?

546
00:53:47,432 --> 00:53:48,934
- Let them go.
- Yes.

547
00:54:01,321 --> 00:54:03,531
Have a drink.

548
00:54:07,243 --> 00:54:09,287
I'm counting on you.

549
00:54:10,163 --> 00:54:11,873
Well, brother!

550
00:54:15,460 --> 00:54:16,544
Greet them.

551
00:54:19,297 --> 00:54:21,341
I'm Yeon Nam-saeng,
Grand General of Goguryeo!

552
00:54:25,136 --> 00:54:28,347
Liaodong will be bitterly cold.
Are you well prepared?

553
00:54:28,348 --> 00:54:31,183
It's my heart that's colder,
unable to be with you all.

554
00:54:31,184 --> 00:54:33,061
My body is fine.

555
00:54:34,145 --> 00:54:38,482
If you endure it a little longer,
I'll come to relieve you soon.

556
00:54:38,483 --> 00:54:40,317
You must do that.

557
00:54:40,318 --> 00:54:42,737
Don't forget that.

558
00:54:46,366 --> 00:54:50,077
His Majesty the King and the Crown Prince

559
00:54:50,078 --> 00:54:52,539
have arrived!

560
00:55:29,868 --> 00:55:30,910
Begin.

561
00:55:31,578 --> 00:55:32,412
Yes.

562
00:57:24,941 --> 00:57:26,484
Take their swords!

563
00:57:39,247 --> 00:57:40,081
Stop!

564
00:58:40,683 --> 00:58:45,313
<i>The whole river's waters have turned red</i>

565
00:58:48,775 --> 00:58:55,657
<i>Iron armor and drums face the north wind</i>

566
00:59:04,832 --> 00:59:06,251
FOREST NEAR SEORABEOL

567
00:59:11,673 --> 00:59:14,509
O Great Jivaka, King of Physicians,

568
00:59:15,760 --> 00:59:17,636
Boy of the Snowy Mountains!

569
00:59:17,637 --> 00:59:22,892
The era of a sick queen
with no heirs is coming to an end.

570
00:59:23,810 --> 00:59:29,606
Let the Jingol gathered here,
who purely inherit Silla's blood,

571
00:59:29,607 --> 00:59:32,610
succeed to the throne!

572
00:59:33,861 --> 00:59:38,448
Punish the incompetent queen
who plunged Silla into crisis

573
00:59:38,449 --> 00:59:42,370
and her nephew Kim Chun-chu,

574
00:59:43,079 --> 00:59:46,873
and show us that only pure-blood Jingol

575
00:59:46,874 --> 00:59:53,089
can fully protect this Silla!

576
00:59:55,091 --> 00:59:59,053
Here, we offer the loyal general

577
00:59:59,637 --> 01:00:04,267
Baek-ryong as a sacrifice!

578
01:00:09,522 --> 01:00:10,356
Grab it.

579
01:00:21,618 --> 01:00:22,952
King Jinpyeong

580
01:00:23,953 --> 01:00:26,663
claimed only their bloodline was Seonggol

581
01:00:26,664 --> 01:00:28,832
and kept the throne in his family
for generations.

582
01:00:28,833 --> 01:00:32,753
He dreamed in vain
that his future son would be Maitreya,

583
01:00:32,754 --> 01:00:36,674
but having no son, he made
his daughter king. How cunning!

584
01:00:38,843 --> 01:00:40,637
In the first place, King Jinheung

585
01:00:41,220 --> 01:00:43,973
accepted Kim Yu-sin's Gaya family
as Jingol

586
01:00:44,974 --> 01:00:46,893
and muddied Silla's bloodline.

587
01:00:47,852 --> 01:00:50,146
Chun-chu is colluding with Kim Yu-sin.

588
01:00:50,813 --> 01:00:54,484
He clearly means to cast us out
and seize the throne!

589
01:00:59,489 --> 01:01:01,699
Is anyone here backing out?

590
01:01:02,200 --> 01:01:03,743
None!

591
01:01:07,747 --> 01:01:09,999
Win over all the remaining Jingol.

592
01:01:11,125 --> 01:01:12,794
Isolate the Queen

593
01:01:13,544 --> 01:01:16,881
so that, to survive, they take my hand,
not Chun-chu's.

594
01:01:17,632 --> 01:01:18,841
Yes.

595
01:02:07,682 --> 01:02:11,978
Dismiss Minister of Defense Kim Chun-chu!

596
01:02:12,687 --> 01:02:16,899
Dismiss Minister of Defense Kim Chun-chu!

597
01:02:18,025 --> 01:02:21,904
Dismiss Minister of Defense Kim Chun-chu!

598
01:02:22,488 --> 01:02:24,532
I have a question for Kim Chun-chu!

599
01:02:25,116 --> 01:02:27,534
I hear General Baek-ryong,
gravely wounded,

600
01:02:27,535 --> 01:02:29,495
went to your house.

601
01:02:31,414 --> 01:02:33,291
A matter this grave,

602
01:02:34,751 --> 01:02:37,587
why did you not report it
to Her Majesty at once?

603
01:02:43,009 --> 01:02:45,386
It is true that General Baek-ryong
came to my home,

604
01:02:46,137 --> 01:02:49,723
but amid Baekje's massive offensive,

605
01:02:49,724 --> 01:02:51,726
to prevent even greater chaos,

606
01:02:52,894 --> 01:02:54,186
I merely acted with caution.

607
01:02:54,187 --> 01:02:56,606
Did you say "with caution"?

608
01:02:57,273 --> 01:03:00,359
With rumors even of betrayal by those
of Gaya descent spreading,

609
01:03:00,943 --> 01:03:02,068
did you not think

610
01:03:02,069 --> 01:03:06,157
the Minister's silence
would only throw Silla into chaos?

611
01:03:12,705 --> 01:03:13,539
This...

612
01:03:15,583 --> 01:03:18,586
is the helmet
General Baek-ryong last wore.

613
01:03:24,550 --> 01:03:28,805
It was found in a coffin
buried by the Minister's retainers.

614
01:03:36,020 --> 01:03:37,563
Did you kill General Baek-ryong?

615
01:03:50,076 --> 01:03:51,410
General Baek-ryong...

616
01:03:52,453 --> 01:03:53,996
Because of his own hatred,

617
01:03:54,705 --> 01:03:58,876
he suspected those of Gaya descent
without evidence and caused chaos,

618
01:04:00,211 --> 01:04:01,920
and failed to defend his fortress.

619
01:04:01,921 --> 01:04:03,923
Is that why you killed him?!

620
01:04:17,812 --> 01:04:18,646
I...

621
01:04:30,199 --> 01:04:31,993
Behead him!

622
01:04:32,577 --> 01:04:35,580
Behead Kim Chun-chu!

623
01:04:42,461 --> 01:04:46,465
Dismiss Minister of Defense Kim Chun-chu!

624
01:04:47,133 --> 01:04:49,844
Dismiss Minister of Defense Kim Chun-chu...

625
01:04:59,312 --> 01:05:00,396
Your Majesty.

626
01:05:01,272 --> 01:05:05,484
Any more hesitation
will only throw Silla into deeper chaos.

627
01:05:06,986 --> 01:05:08,863
Dismiss Minister of Defense Kim Chun-chu

628
01:05:09,655 --> 01:05:11,239
and behead him!

629
01:05:11,240 --> 01:05:12,366
Behead him!

630
01:05:12,950 --> 01:05:15,660
Behead Kim Chun-chu!

631
01:05:15,661 --> 01:05:17,495
Behead him!

632
01:05:17,496 --> 01:05:20,206
Behead Kim Chun-chu!

633
01:05:20,207 --> 01:05:21,750
Behead him!

634
01:05:21,751 --> 01:05:23,836
Behead Kim Chun-chu!

635
01:05:24,503 --> 01:05:26,004
Behead him!

636
01:05:26,005 --> 01:05:28,966
Behead Kim Chun-chu!

637
01:05:29,675 --> 01:05:32,219
General Kim Yu-sin has arrived!

638
01:06:14,637 --> 01:06:16,806
KIM YU-SIN (SILLA SENIOR GENERAL)

639
01:06:31,862 --> 01:06:34,280
Now, go far away.

640
01:06:34,281 --> 01:06:35,992
- Far away!
- Your Majesty.

641
01:06:36,867 --> 01:06:41,080
May I give one last farewell address?

642
01:06:43,791 --> 01:06:45,584
Father!

643
01:06:53,050 --> 01:06:53,884
Oh, my.

644
01:07:02,351 --> 01:07:03,519
First of all,

645
01:07:04,687 --> 01:07:08,523
seeing you all cheer me on as I depart
for Liaodong so warmly,

646
01:07:08,524 --> 01:07:10,650
my gratitude is as vast as the sea,

647
01:07:10,651 --> 01:07:14,447
yet somehow I feel I am being driven out.

648
01:07:21,662 --> 01:07:22,496
Now.

649
01:07:30,004 --> 01:07:31,297
Attention!

650
01:07:39,180 --> 01:07:40,306
I, Yeon Gaesomun,

651
01:07:42,058 --> 01:07:45,019
have thought about what's best
for the people of Goguryeo,

652
01:07:45,603 --> 01:07:46,771
and thought

653
01:07:47,438 --> 01:07:49,440
again and again.

654
01:07:50,483 --> 01:07:51,567
And I...

655
01:07:54,904 --> 01:07:56,072
have reached a conclusion.

656
01:08:02,078 --> 01:08:06,415
To the people who gave their lives
to protect this land, today's Goguryeo

657
01:08:07,750 --> 01:08:08,584
is a disgrace!

658
01:08:12,546 --> 01:08:14,799
The ultimate disgrace!

659
01:08:19,929 --> 01:08:21,430
Our Goguryeo

660
01:08:22,348 --> 01:08:23,516
never bows its head

661
01:08:24,809 --> 01:08:26,435
to anyone!

662
01:09:03,931 --> 01:09:07,143
As long as I, Yeon Gaesomun, am alive,

663
01:09:09,145 --> 01:09:12,231
no one can ever...

664
01:09:17,820 --> 01:09:20,990
violate our Goguryeo!

665
01:09:45,472 --> 01:09:47,975
Treason!

666
01:10:22,801 --> 01:10:24,803
THANKS TO JO SEONG-HA
FOR HIS SPECIAL APPEARANCE

667
01:10:50,246 --> 01:10:55,251
Subtitle translation by: Mongshilkim
